Two Ways of Adding Constraints

First Approach: During table creation
You can put the constraint directly beside the column:

CREATE TABLE users (
    id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    email VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE
);

Here UNIQUE is attached directly to email.

Second Approach:(Manual add constraint)  After table creation

You can add a constraint separately:

ALTER TABLE users
ADD CONSTRAINT unique_email UNIQUE(email);

Both approaches are valid.
The second form is useful when the table already exists.
It means we can add condition on any column that he has to first fullfill our criteria before adding data

