DISTINCT Keyword

DISTINCT is used to return only unique values.
SELECT DISTINCT gender FROM users;//normally without distinct answer was al lot of males,females of each record,by using distinct ,it gives the unique/1 time value from all values

Example 2:
SELECT DISTINCT gender, salary
FROM users;

Now it removes duplicate gender + salary combinations, not duplicates of gender alone

Explanation:
DISTINCT does not independently remove duplicate genders or duplicate salaries.
Instead, it removes duplicate combinations of the selected columns.

Think of it as:

"Give me each unique gender + salary combination."

